---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/ai.css';
---

<Layout
  title="DeepSeek Flash — A.I. — Rycode"
  description="Current recommended DeepSeek API model. API id deepseek-flash. Model version DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash."
  variant="ai"
>
  <article class="ai-model">
    <p class="ai-model-kicker">DeepSeek · current</p>
    <h1 class="ai-model-title">Flash</h1>
    <p class="ai-model-dek">API id: <code>deepseek-flash</code>. Model version on Models &amp; Pricing (fetched 21 Sep 2026): <strong>DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash</strong>. This is DeepSeek’s current recommended API model. Legacy names <code>deepseek-v4-flash</code> and <code>deepseek-v4-flash-vision-exp</code> still route here and bill at Flash prices.</p>
    <hr class="ai-model-rule" />

    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Training</h2>
    <p>Company announce (10 Sep 2026): 552B-parameter MoE; new Causal Encoder–Decoder architecture with 8B active parameters for input and 16B for output; larger-scale RL post-training. Full dataset mix and FLOPs table: UNKNOWN on the pricing page. Knowledge cutoff: UNKNOWN on the pricing page.</p>

    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Inference</h2>
    <p>Thinking mode on by default; non-thinking available. Native vision (pricing table: Vision ✓). Tool calls, JSON output, Responses API, Anthropic-compatible API. FIM completion: non-thinking only (beta).</p>

    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Context</h2>
    <p>1M token context. Max output 384K (pricing page).</p>

    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Methods</h2>
    <p>Dual thinking / non-thinking. Effort: <code>low</code> / <code>high</code> / <code>max</code> (docs). Exact train-time RL recipe beyond “larger-scale RL post-training”: UNKNOWN.</p>

    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Benchmarking</h2>
    <p>Announce claims vendor results ahead of flagship models including DeepSeek-V4-Pro. Changelog (10 Sep 2026) prints a vendor eval list for V4.1-Flash. Independent Arena / HLE tables: do not invent. Prefer DeepSeek’s own changelog or tech report if you quote a number.</p>

    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Hardware</h2>
    <p>KV cache claim vs prior gen (vendor announce): 1/4 HBM and 1/8 SSD storage. Training cluster size: UNKNOWN. Open weights: <a href="https://huggingface.co/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash">huggingface.co/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash</a>.</p>

    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Access and pricing (vendor)</h2>
    <p>Copied from Models &amp; Pricing, 21 Sep 2026. Per 1M tokens. Off-peak is half of peak. Peak hours: 01:00–04:00 and 06:00–10:00 UTC, Monday–Friday, excluding Chinese public holidays. Concurrency limit listed: 2500.</p>
    <div class="ai-model-table-wrap">
      <table class="ai-model-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Band</th>
            <th scope="col">Off-peak</th>
            <th scope="col">Peak</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Input cache hit</td><td>$0.003</td><td>$0.006</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Input cache miss</td><td>$0.15</td><td>$0.30</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Output</td><td>$0.60</td><td>$1.20</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>Re-check the live pricing page before you quote a dollar.</p>

    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Sources</h2>
    <ul class="ai-model-sources">
      <li><a href="https://api-docs.deepseek.com/quick_start/pricing">Models &amp; Pricing</a> (fetched 21 Sep 2026)</li>
      <li><a href="https://api-docs.deepseek.com/news/news260910">DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash announce</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://api-docs.deepseek.com/updates">Change log</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://api-docs.deepseek.com/guides/thinking_mode/">Thinking mode</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://huggingface.co/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash">Hugging Face: DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash</a></li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</Layout>
